WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.908
Theo holds a Maryland license.

00:00:01.908 --> 00:00:04.961
An insurer now offers AMG a producer agreement.

00:00:04.961 --> 00:00:09.158
Three documents are in play, and they are not the same.

00:00:09.158 --> 00:00:14.119
The license is the state’s permission to act as a producer in Maryland.

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:19.079
The producer agreement is the business contract setting commissions, duties and termination terms.

00:00:19.079 --> 00:00:22.895
The appointment is the insurer’s registration of Theo as its

00:00:22.895 --> 00:00:26.711
agent, recorded in the insurer’s producer register under Maryland law.

00:00:26.711 --> 00:00:32.053
A producer may hold a license and a contract and still lack an appointment.

00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:35.487
Only the appointment makes him the insurer’s agent for

00:00:35.487 --> 00:00:38.540
the acts the statute requires an appointment for.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.074
Appointments attach to people and to entities.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:45.419
The insurer appoints AMG, the business entity, and it appoints each individual

00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:49.764
producer who will act for it; an agency appointment does not by

00:00:49.764 --> 00:00:53.385
itself make every employee an appointed agent of the insurer.

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:56.281
Theo should confirm that his own name is

00:00:56.281 --> 00:00:58.815
in the insurer’s register, not only AMG’s.

00:00:58.815 --> 00:01:02.798
When a producer leaves one agency for another, the appointment through

00:01:02.798 --> 00:01:06.419
the old agency ends and a new appointment is needed.

00:01:06.419 --> 00:01:10.039
Appointment is also line-specific: an appointment for life business does

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:13.660
not authorize health solicitation unless the insurer’s register covers it.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:17.221
Maryland lets a licensed producer solicit an application for an

00:01:17.221 --> 00:01:20.427
insurer authorized for that line without first being appointed.

00:01:20.427 --> 00:01:24.344
The protection kicks in when the insurer accepts the application: within

00:01:24.344 --> 00:01:28.262
30 days it must either reject the application or appoint the

00:01:28.262 --> 00:01:31.467
producer and enter the required information in its register.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:36.453
So Theo may bring a first health application to a carrier he has never

00:01:36.453 --> 00:01:41.439
worked with, but the carrier may not keep accepting his business without appointing him.

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:44.645
Accepting an application for processing is not acceptance of

00:01:44.645 --> 00:01:47.850
the risk and does not mean coverage has begun.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.248
Once it appoints Theo, the insurer enters the appointment in its producer register within

00:01:52.248 --> 00:01:56.333
30 days and gives him written documentation of the appointment within 30 days.

00:01:56.333 --> 00:02:00.731
Theo keeps that documentation and a list of every insurer that has appointed him.

00:02:00.731 --> 00:02:03.873
With the written documentation in hand he may act within

00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:06.700
his authority even before the register entry is complete.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.156
Appointment records stay available while the appointment is active and for

00:02:10.156 --> 00:02:13.612
at least five years after it ends, and electronic records must

00:02:13.612 --> 00:02:16.754
be retrievable within ten working days of the Commissioner’s request.

00:02:16.754 --> 00:02:20.210
A screenshot no one can find later is not a record.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.887
An insurer that terminates an appointment updates its

00:02:22.887 --> 00:02:25.563
register within 30 days after the effective date.

00:02:25.563 --> 00:02:29.578
If the termination is for a reason that could be grounds for

00:02:29.578 --> 00:02:33.593
discipline, the insurer must also notify the Commissioner, send Theo a copy

00:02:33.593 --> 00:02:37.607
within 15 days after that notice, and Theo then has 30 days

00:02:37.607 --> 00:02:41.622
after receiving it to submit comments, with a copy to the insurer.

00:02:41.622 --> 00:02:44.968
Once his appointment ends he must cease soliciting for that

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:48.313
insurer immediately; a pending commission does not extend his authority.

00:02:48.313 --> 00:02:51.659
Ending an appointment is the insurer’s decision and does not

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:54.670
revoke his license; only the Commissioner can do that.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:59.070
Theo’s license stays valid even if no insurer has appointed him.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:03.870
He may keep it active through renewal and continuing education and may

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:08.670
solicit applications that an insurer must then accept and appoint or reject.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.870
What he may not do is hold himself out as an insurer’s agent,

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:19.070
bind coverage or collect premium for an insurer that has not appointed him.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:23.870
For every appointment question, name the actor and the clock: the producer

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:28.670
solicits; the insurer accepts, appoints within 30 days, documents within 30 days,

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.470
keeps records five years, and on termination updates the register within 30

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:37.070
days and notifies the Commissioner when discipline grounds exist.
